## Intent → widgets

| Intent | Flutter |
|---|---|
| `screen` + `scroll-v` | `Scaffold(body: SingleChildScrollView(padding: EdgeInsets.all(16.sdp), child: Column(...)))` |
| `stack-v` / `stack-h` with gap | `Column(spacing: 12.sdp)` / `Row(spacing: 8.sdp)` (Flutter ≥ 3.27), or `SizedBox(height: 12.sdp)` separators |
| `overlay` | `Stack` + `Positioned`/`Align` (only for true overlays) |
| `list` | `ListView.separated(padding: EdgeInsets.all(16.sdp), separatorBuilder: (_, __) => SizedBox(height: 8.sdp), …)` |
| `grid` | `GridView.builder(gridDelegate: SliverGridDelegateWithMaxCrossAxisExtent(maxCrossAxisExtent: 200.sdp, mainAxisSpacing: 12.sdp, crossAxisSpacing: 12.sdp))` |
| `carousel` | `ListView.builder(scrollDirection: Axis.horizontal)` or `PageView` / `CarouselView` for paged |
| `card` | `Card(shape: RoundedRectangleBorder(borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(12.sdp)), child: Padding(padding: EdgeInsets.all(16.sdp), …))` |
| `sizing: fill` / `hug` | `Expanded` / `Flexible` / `double.infinity` width · default |
| `sizing: ratio` | `AspectRatio(aspectRatio: 4 / 3, child: …)` |
| `sizing: clamp` | `ConstrainedBox(constraints: BoxConstraints(minWidth: 280, maxWidth: 600))` `// ad:fixed clamp` |
| `truncate` | `Text(maxLines: 2, overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis)` |
| `divider` | `Divider(thickness: 1, height: 1)` `// ad:fixed hairline` |
| touch target | visual size as a token + hit area via Material `minimumSize: Size(48, 48)` / `kMinInteractiveDimension` on the button style or a `SizedBox` hit box `// ad:fixed touch-min` — never clamp the visual |
| `adapt` | `LayoutBuilder` / `MediaQuery.sizeOf(context).shortestSide >= 600` for structure; facilitators `.sdpQualifier`, `.sdpScreen` for values |

Typography: put sizes in `ThemeData.textTheme` built inside the provider (`TextStyle(fontSize: 16.ssp)`), so the theme is rebuilt when the snapshot changes.

## Custom strategies (`appdimens_custom`, unreleased)

Full decision flow, cross-platform syntax table, rules and kit checks: `appdimens-custom-strategies`.

Only when `appdimens.config.json` declares `customStrategies` (or the user asks for their own strategy). Use the declared ids, never invent one; see the decision table → *Project-defined strategies*. Free-form formulas (`"type": "expression"`, `"formula"`) live in the JSON file.

Simplest strategy, when the user just wants to write the math: one typed closure, autocompleted:

```dart
final product = customScaleStrategy((s) => s.clamp(s.width / 360, 0.85, 1.8)); // factor: once per window
final hud = scalingFormulaOf((s) => s.base * s.pow(s.sw / 360, 0.8));         // final value (base = the value passed)
SizedBox(width: 48.cdpWith(product));
```

Scope names match the text language: `base` (formula only) `sw width height shortSide longSide diagonal perimeter aspectRatio ratio density fontScale device`, flags `phone tablet desktop tv watch car vr landscape portrait multiWindow`, math `pow sqrt ln log10 exp abs round min max clamp lerp smoothstep`. Inline text: `16.cdpFormula('base * (sw / 360)')`, `context.cdpFormula(16, '…')`. For JSON or remote config, the same formula as text: `{"id": "hud", "formula": "base * pow(sw / 360, 0.8)"}` (shaped `base * (…)` it costs one multiply). Check numbers with `appdimens-kit custom explain --formula "<text>" --devices …`.

```dart
// pubspec: appdimens_custom (or appdimens_bom)
import 'package:appdimens_custom/appdimens_custom.dart';

ScalingStrategies.loadJson(await rootBundle.loadString('assets/appdimens-strategies.json'));
final brand = ScalingStrategies.getOrThrow('brand');
Padding(padding: EdgeInsets.all(16.cdpWith(brand)), child: Text('Hi', style: TextStyle(fontSize: 14.cspWith(brand))));
ScalingStrategyScope(strategy: brand, child: …)   // then context.cdp(16) / context.csp(14)
```

## Lint (what `appdimens-kit lint` flags here)

- `EdgeInsets.all(16)`, `EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 16)`, `SizedBox(height: 16)`, `BorderRadius.circular(12)`, `fontSize: 16` numeric literals > 2 → tokens.
- Strategy token without its package import (`.asdp` without `appdimens_auto`).
- Deprecated 2.x `fx` / `dy` APIs (see upstream MIGRATION.md).

